Memorandum of today's call attached. Participants were Vasseur-Kyle, Penhal=
igon and Tirado for Marchwood; Achterberg, Raghunathan and me for the staff=
.<br />
<br />
Marchwood did not concede the legal point and I did not press them to. What=
 they did agree to is the substance: the 214 accounts move to Signal Peak T=
rust Company under an arrangement with no adviser withdrawal authority, the=
 direct fee-debit instruction stops firm-wide, and the treatment carries fo=
rward to acquired and newly onboarded accounts. Tirado asked whether an und=
ertaking in those terms would close the examination and Rosalind said it wo=
uld, subject to the letter actually saying so.<br />
<br />
Vasseur-Kyle said she would have the letter to us this week.<br />
<br />
Desmond
